+
+## Patch 17 — Polished Crystal wild encounters
+- `PolishedCrystalRomHandler`: `getEncounters`/`setEncounters` over the eight grass/surf tables (morn/day/nite
+  sets, or the day set written to all three), swarms, the 15 fishing groups (one set per distinct rod list),
+  the headbutt/rock-smash sets and the bug contest. Writes are same-size and in place: a changed Pokemon
+  rewrites only the slot's two species bytes (NO_FORM, as plain `wildmon` rows carry); a level byte changes
+  only when a level setting changed it and never when it is a LEVEL_FROM_BADGES encoding. Formed slots and
+  fishing's species-0 time rows are kept out of the model, so they are never written. EGG, the unused $100,
+  Unown and every variant form are banned from wild pools; `hasTimeBasedEncounters` is on. Every other
+  writer still throws.
+- `config/polished_offsets.ini` supplement: `FishGroupCount`, `TreeMonSetCount`, `ContestMonCount`.
diff --git a/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini b/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini
index 898f7b2..93baeb4 100644
--- a/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini
+++ b/src/com/dabomstew/pkrandom/config/polished_offsets.ini
@@ -721,3 +721,6 @@ Version=50                     // ROM 0x14C = $32; the generated block says 0
 CRCInHeader=0xA36C             // ROM 0x14E-0x14F read big-endian as UPR does; the generated block has it byte-swapped
 VariantFormTableOffset=0x3E7C  // VariantSpeciesAndFormTable 00:3e7c (data/pokemon/variant_forms.asm), 2-byte dp per form
 VariantFormCount=46            // NUM_VARIANT_FORMS = $2e: BaseData/EvosAttacksPointers records 292..337
+FishGroupCount=15              // NUM_FISHGROUPS (constants/map_data_constants.asm:68): FishGroups rows
+TreeMonSetCount=10             // NUM_TREEMON_SETS (constants/pokemon_data_constants.asm:381); the last (ROCK) has no rare list
+ContestMonCount=12             // (ContestMonsEnd 25:58f0 - ContestMons 25:58b4) / 5; ContestMons has no terminator
